            <ArticleTitle>Morphological Evaluation of the Influence of the Peptide Complex from Tissue of Porcine Kidneys on the Experimental Urolithiasis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>207-210</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s10517-017-3959-8</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We performed morphological analysis of the effect of the peptide complex from porcine kidneys on the course of experimental urolithiasis modeled in rats by treatment with 1% ethylene glycol solution (in drinking water) for 6 weeks. The peptide complex obtained by acetic acid extraction was administered in a dose of 15 mg. Administration of the peptide complex to animals with experimental kidney stone disease leads to 100% destruction of large and medium stones to the &quot;dust&quot; granularity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
